          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Awards and Honors</strong><br>\nGordon Moore has received numerous awards and honors for his work, including the Presidential Medal of Freedom, the United States' highest civilian honor, in 2002. He has been recognized for his pioneering contributions to science and technology and for his leadership in the semiconductor industry.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Post-Retirement Activities</strong><br>\nAfter retiring from active duty at Intel, Moore continued to influence the field as an emeritus board member. He remains a respected authority in semiconductor technology and innovation, providing insight and guidance on emerging trends.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and the Future</strong><br>\nMoore's legacy extends beyond his prediction. It encompasses a shift in how society uses and perceives technology. His foresight into the exponential growth of computing power continues to shape research, development, and strategic planning in the tech industry well into the 21st century.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
